      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Prompt-only compaction never records usage",
      "description": "The prompt-only path calls the SDK query and returns an `ActionResult` without usage metadata; unlike the session path, it also never requires a `UsageCapture`. Since `COMPACT` is counted as an LLM action by `sq stats run`, these calls will always appear as unrecorded, even when they spend tokens. Capture and attach usage on this path, or explicitly exclude it from the report\u2019s LLM-action accounting.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "src/squadron/pipeline/actions/compact.py:107-166"
    },
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Failed SDK compaction drops captured spend",
      "description": "If `compact()` raises after dispatch has accumulated telemetry, the broad handler returns a failed result without reading telemetry from the exception or stamping a usage record. This loses spend from failed compactions, contrary to the failure-recording behavior implemented for other LLM actions. Add a regression test for a failed compaction carrying telemetry.",
      "file_ref": null,
